+  def deliver_later
+    Webhook::DeliveryJob.perform_later(self)
+  end
+
+  # Delivers at most once: the delivery is atomically claimed (pending ->
+  # in_progress) before the request is made, so a retried or duplicated job
+  # finds nothing to claim and sends nothing. Since it is only ever created
+  # once per webhook and event, the POST goes out exactly once.
